From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the boot also builds the records made with the other EDEN_NX2_MASK_COMPONENTS mode, keyed for this mode (EDEN_UP_BOOT_ALL_STATES=1), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_BOOT_ALL_STATES=1 (exact "1", read once at boot).

Why: the boot's load_graphics leaves out every record whose dynamic-state bits differ from this
device's. In the T151 play session of 13 Nov that was 3,127 of the 5,433 graphics records of
vulkan.bin and vulkan_mesh.bin ("3127 not taken by the boot (3127 for another dynamic state ...);
recorded otherwise: ... mask components 3127", every other bit 0): records written while
EDEN_NX2_MASK_COMPONENTS was off. The play env has it on now (env-play-v31). Those states are
never built at boot, and a draw that needs one makes it as "new" (506 "new" builds in that session,
the slowest ones: 14.7 ms each on the GPU thread on average plus a driver compile without a driver
cache entry). INFERRED, not checked: how many of the 506 are such records (the console's files
were not read for this; the line below tells it on the next boot).

What: the mask mode is one bit of the key (FixedPipelineState::mask_components, set from the
switch alone in Refresh; no other field depends on it). It only changes the colour write mask the
pipeline is built with (vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp: write_mask &= fragment_color_components); the
translation does not read it. So such a record, with the bit set to this mode, is exactly the key a
draw here makes for the same state. With the switch, after the boot's own pass (and after the
EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS legacy pass), a second pass reads vulkan.bin and vulkan_mesh.bin again with
VideoCommon::ReadPipelines (the reader that never cuts a file back) and, for records that differ
ONLY in the mask bit and have this driver id and version: sets the bit, skips the key if
disk_pipelines has it (the same state was recorded in this mode too) or the pass met it already,
then goes the same way as a record of the first pass (used-list filter unless
EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES=1, then queued on the builders, NotePrepared for
EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP). Records that differ in any other bit stay out (those bits change what the
key's other fields mean). The rekeyed keys are NOT put in disk_pipelines: if a draw makes one at run
time (after an eviction), it is reported as "new" and its record is written in this mode, exactly
as with the switch off, so the files converge and turning the switch off later loses nothing.
One line: "EDEN_UP_BOOT_ALL_STATES=1: <r> records of the other mask components mode read, <t> taken
under this mode's key and built now, <w> already on disk in this mode, <o> for another dynamic
state or driver, <n> not in the used list". The condition of the first pass moved into a lambda
(other_state), same expression, same order.

Cost: the boot reads the two files again (122 + 62 MB in the 13 Nov backup) and builds <t> more
pipelines on the builders. T151's boot built 2,571 in about 14.6 s (8.1 to 22.7 s); if all 3,127
are taken that is up to about 18 s more, if half are twins about 9 s (INFERRED from that rate; a
driver compile without a driver-cache entry is slower than the boot's mostly cached ones). Driver
memory for the extra pipelines (about 0.45 MB each by the code's own estimate) until the first
eviction check after 9000 frames frees the unused ones; with 0685's EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES=1
they stay. The driver cache file grows by their entries. PrepareKept's stats still count these
records as "not taken by the boot (... for another dynamic state)" (it looks up the recorded key).

Off: the first pass's condition is the same expression (now a lambda); one bool test per record
and one load of a static per boot. Not in the kept-store stamp (no translation changes).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 246a788..6559efb 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -1335,6 +1335,20 @@ KeepBoot KeepBootPipelines() {
     }();
     return mode;
